<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Greek-Turkish EEZ Conflict - Greek Human, 2021</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY text=#dcdcdc bgColor=#2b2b2b scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;CMO: The Greek-Turkish EEZ Conflict, 2021&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Al "Beirutdude" Sandrik&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;The Time Is: 25 March, 2021 00:00:00 Zulu/02:00:00 Athens Time&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;AOR: Greece, Aegean Sea, Turkey &amp;amp; Eastern Mediterranean Sea &lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;Playable as the Greek side only&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;2 Days Duration&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In late November, 2019 a diplomatic crisis erupted between Greece and Turkey when Turkey announced it had signed a memorandum of understanding with　Libya　outlining their maritime boundaries. This particular dispute, amongst all of the other conflicts simmering between the two rivals involved an agreement between Turkey and Libya that defined oil right for a newly found oil field in an area Greece claimed as part of its Maritime Zone (MZ). &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;At stake is national prestige - and the lucrative prospect of hydrocarbon resources. Greece and Turkey had not delimited their Exclusive Economic Zones (EEZs), which allow countries to exploit undersea wealth. Alarmed by Turkish statements that Ankara would send ships to look for oil and gas in its newly claimed dominions, Greece declared a 200 nm EEZ around its islands, reinforced its military forces on Crete, and declared to Ankara that any trespassing drill ships would be sunk. "If a Turkish drill ship does show up, our ships would take action against it, and that could lead to an armed confrontation, because these ships are accompanied by naval vessels. And of course, that would lead to war," stated a veteran senior diplomat on condition of anonymity.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;"There will be no Turkish drill ship. It has been communicated to Turkey that we shall not tolerate any exploration in the area Greece considers to be its EEZ," says International public law professor Angelos Syrigos, who also serves as an MP for the ruling conservative New Democracy party.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Undeterred by Turkish military strength Greek Defense Minister Nikos Panayotopoulos told reporters, "We are preparing for all eventualities on all levels." The Hellenic Navy's chief of staff, Admiral Nikos Tsounis, later added: "We shall not wait for anyone to come and help us. Whatever we do, we shall do alone."&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;In early March of 2021 Ankara decided it was time to test Greek resolve and began exploration in mid-March. On March 23rd, Athens announced any Turkish exploration vessels and their escorts still within the declared EEZ after 00:00 utc 25 March 2021 (Independence Day) would be subject to immediate military action.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Note:&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Be sure to find all of your airbases as some a colocated with SAMS and Radars.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT color=red&gt;I have set up naval missions and some air missions but they are "scrubed for humans,"&amp;nbsp;If you want to use them in your play, you can activate them in the Scenario Editor. For that reason the mission reference points are still on the map. Otherwise, just select all of the RPs and delete them to set up your own missions.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Originally created under CMO Version 1.01 Build 1134.1 &lt;FONT face="Courier New"&gt;&lt;FONT face="Courier New"&gt;&lt;FONT face="Times New Roman"&gt;– Data Base: DB3000 483&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Times New Roman"&gt;An .INI and Delta File have both been provided for rebuilds&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Times New Roman"&gt;Al "BeirutDude" Sandrik (ex-Beachinnole)&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT face="Times New Roman"&gt;Al.Sandrik@gmail.com&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
